Replication materials for "Humans show limited ability to distinguish
human-authored and AI-generated political content on social media"
(Paik, Ventura, Ansell, Bode, Toney-Wails, Singh)

Two licenses apply, by folder.

1. DATA AND DOCUMENTATION (data/, output/, README.md, codebook.md): CC0 1.0

   To the extent possible under law, the authors have waived all copyright
   and related or neighboring rights to the survey data, Bradley-Terry
   scores, text-feature labels, generated figures and tables, README and
   codebook in this package. Full text:
   https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

   Third-party content. The human-authored posts in data/ (columns such as
   Text, post, post_left, post_right and the *_selected_*_posts.csv files)
   were collected from X/Twitter, YouTube, TikTok and Truth Social. The
   authors claim no rights over that text; it remains the property of its
   original authors and is subject to the terms of the platforms it was
   collected from. User handles have been replaced by @USER. The CC0 waiver
   covers the authors' compilation, annotations and derived variables only.
   The AI-generated posts were produced by the authors with OpenAI and Meta
   Llama models and are covered by the waiver.

   Respondent data are de-identified: direct identifiers, IP addresses,
   geolocation and free-text feedback were removed, and panel identifiers
   were replaced by hashed keys. Please do not attempt to re-identify
   participants.

